# Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 — the charity test

## Article 1 and Article 2 — the interpretation provisions the test needs

<!-- l4: decide:Article 1 — the definitions on which the charity test depends -->

**1.** Article 1 — the definitions on which the charity test depends if—

    (a) "charitable purpose" has the meaning given by Article 6;;

    (b) "constitution" has the meaning given by Article 2(4);;

    (c) "governor" in relation to an entity (including a registered charity) has the meaning given by Article 2(7);;

    (d) "Minister" means the Minister for External Relations;; and

    (e) "purpose", in relation to an entity, has the meaning given by Article 2(6);.

<!-- l4: decide:Article 2(4) — constitution -->

**2.** Article 2(4) — constitution if—

    (a) (4) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, "constitution" in relation to an entity means –;

    (b) (a) in the case of a trust the terms of the trust;;

    (c) (d) in the case of a foundation, the charter and regulations of the foundation;;

    (d) (e) in the case of a company, the memorandum and articles of association of the company;; and

    (e) (g) in any other case, any instrument or instruments (in whatever form) that establish the entity or give it any powers..

<!-- l4: decide:Article 2(6) — purpose -->

**3.** Article 2(6) — purpose if—

    (a) (6) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, "purpose" in relation to an entity means –;

    (b) (c) in the case of a foundation, the objects specified in its charter or its regulations; or; and

    (c) (d) in the case of any other entity, a purpose to which that entity's property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)..

<!-- l4: decide:Article 2(7) — governor -->

**4.** Article 2(7) — governor if—

    (a) (7) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, "governor" in relation to an entity means –;

    (b) (a) in the case of a trust or fidéicommis, a trustee or fidéicommissaire of the trust or fidéicommis;;

    (c) (b) in the case of a foundation, a member of the council of the foundation;;

    (d) (c) in the case of a company, a director of the company;; and

    (e) (e) in any other case, a person who, under the constitution of the entity, has the general control and management of the administration of the entity..

## The ontology

<!-- l4: declare:Purpose -->

**5.** In this Act, “Purpose” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “description”, being a STRING;

    (b) “the prevention or relief of poverty”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the advancement of education”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “the advancement of religion”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “the advancement of health”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “the saving of lives”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “the advancement of citizenship or community development”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “rural or urban regeneration”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (l) “the advancement of public participation in sport”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “sport that involves physical skill and exertion”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “the provision of recreational facilities, or the organisation of recreational activities, with the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (r) “the promotion of religious or racial harmony”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (s) “the promotion of equality and diversity”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (t) “the advancement of environmental protection or improvement”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “the advancement of animal welfare”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (w) “reasonably regarded as analogous to any of the purposes listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (o)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (x) “the advancement of a philosophical belief (whether or not involving belief in a god)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (y) “for advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election to any office, whether in Jersey or elsewhere”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (z) “purely ancillary or incidental to any of the entity's charitable purposes”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:Constitution -->

**6.** In this Act, “Constitution” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “description”, being a STRING;

    (b) “express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a Minister”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a member of the States Assembly”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a Minister”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a member of the States Assembly”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “express permission for any of the entity's governors to be any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (h) “that permission extended to such a person acting in that capacity”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:PublicBenefitFinding -->

**7.** In this Act, “PublicBenefitFinding” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “description”, being a STRING;

    (b) “public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “benefit provided to a section of the public only”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (i) “a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:Entity -->

**8.** In this Act, “Entity” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “purposes”, being a list of Purpose;

    (c) “constitution”, being a Constitution;

    (d) “an applicant”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “the public benefit finding”, being a PublicBenefitFinding; and

    (f) “specified in an Order under Article 5(3) disapplying paragraph (2)”, being a BOOLEAN.

